{"_meta": {"fetched_at": "2026-06-16T15:09:55.486059+00:00", "url": "https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q8IWZ6.json", "method": "GET", "status": 200}, "_payload": {"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "secondaryAccessions": ["Q4W5P8", "Q8N581", "Q9NVI4"], "uniProtkbId": "BBS7_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2003-11-07", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2006-03-07", "entryVersion": 185, "sequenceVersion": 2}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "BBSome complex member BBS7"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "BBS2-like protein 1"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Bardet-Biedl syndrome 7 protein"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "BBS7"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "BBS2L1"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17574030"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22072986"}], "value": "The BBSome complex is thought to function as a coat complex required for sorting of specific membrane proteins to the primary cilia. The BBSome complex is required for ciliogenesis but is dispensable for centriolar satellite function. This ciliogenic function is mediated in part by the Rab8 GDP/GTP exchange factor, which localizes to the basal body and contacts the BBSome. Rab8(GTP) enters the primary cilium and promotes extension of the ciliary membrane. Firstly the BBSome associates with the ciliary membrane and binds to RAB3IP/Rabin8, the guanosyl exchange factor (GEF) for Rab8 and then the Rab8-GTP localizes to the cilium and promotes docking and fusion of carrier vesicles to the base of the ciliary membrane. The BBSome complex, together with the LTZL1, controls SMO ciliary trafficking and contributes to the sonic hedgehog (SHH) pathway regulation. Required for proper BBSome complex assembly and its ciliary localization"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16327777"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17574030"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18000879"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "20080638"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22072986"}], "value": "Part of BBSome complex, that contains BBS1, BBS2, BBS4, BBS5, BBS7, BBS8/TTC8, BBS9 and BBIP10. Interacts with BBS2 (via C-terminus). Interacts with CCDC28B and ALDOB. Interacts with SMO; the interaction is indicative for the association of SMO with the BBsome complex to facilitate ciliary localization of SMO"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P05062", "geneName": "ALDOB", "intActId": "EBI-1045507"}, "numberOfExperiments": 4, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8NFJ9", "geneName": "BBS1", "intActId": "EBI-1805484"}, "numberOfExperiments": 11, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8TAM1", "geneName": "BBS10", "intActId": "EBI-6128013"}, "numberOfExperiments": 5, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q6ZW61", "geneName": "BBS12", "intActId": "EBI-6128352"}, "numberOfExperiments": 8, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q9BXC9", "geneName": "BBS2", "intActId": "EBI-748297"}, "numberOfExperiments": 17, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P78371", "geneName": "CCT2", "intActId": "EBI-357407"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q15051", "geneName": "IQCB1", "intActId": "EBI-2805823"}, "numberOfExperiments": 5, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6", "intActId": "EBI-1806001"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P05412", "geneName": "JUN", "intActId": "EBI-852823"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IWZ6-2", "intActId": "EBI-20947190"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q9BXC9", "geneName": "BBS2", "intActId": "EBI-748297"}, "numberOfExperiments": 6, "organismDiffer": false}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17574030"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22072986"}], "value": "Cell projection, cilium membrane", "id": "SL-0305"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22072986"}], "value": "Cytoplasm", "id": "SL-0086"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22072986"}], "value": "Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, microtubule organizing center, centrosome, centriolar satellite", "id": "SL-0485"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q8K2G4"}], "value": "Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, cilium basal body", "id": "SL-0087"}}]}, {"commentType": "ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS", "events": ["Alternative splicing"], "isoforms": [{"name": {"value": "1"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "Long"}, {"value": "lBBS2L1"}], "isoformIds": ["Q8IWZ6-1"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Displayed"}, {"name": {"value": "2"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "Short"}, {"value": "sBBS2L1"}], "isoformIds": ["Q8IWZ6-2"], "sequenceIds": ["VSP_008850"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Described"}]}, {"texts": [{"value": "Isoform 2 is ubiquitously expressed. Isoform 1 is expressed in retina, lung, liver, testis, ovary, prostate, small intestine, liver, brain, heart and pancreas"}], "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"}, {"commentType": "DISEASE", "note": {"texts": [{"value": "Ciliary dysfunction leads to a broad spectrum of disorders, collectively termed ciliopathies. Overlapping clinical features include retinal degeneration, renal cystic disease, skeletal abnormalities, fibrosis of various organ, and a complex range of anatomical and functional defects of the central and peripheral nervous system. The ciliopathy range of diseases includes Meckel-Gruber syndrome, Bardet-Biedl syndrome, Joubert syndrome, nephronophtisis, Senior-Loken syndrome, and Jeune asphyxiating thoracic dystrophy among others. Single-locus allelism is insufficient to explain the variable penetrance and expressivity of such disorders, leading to the suggestion that variations across multiple sites of the ciliary proteome, including BBS7, influence the clinical outcome"}]}}, {"commentType": "DISEASE", "disease": {"diseaseId": "Bardet-Biedl syndrome 7", "diseaseAccession": "DI-00165", "acronym": "BBS7", "description": "A syndrome characterized by usually severe pigmentary retinopathy, early-onset obesity, polydactyly, hypogenitalism, renal malformation and intellectual disability. Secondary features include diabetes mellitus, hypertension and congenital heart disease. Bardet-Biedl syndrome inheritance is autosomal recessive, but three mutated alleles (two at one locus, and a third at a second locus) may be required for clinical manifestation of some forms of the disease.", "diseaseCrossReference": {"database": "MIM", "id": "615984"}, "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12567324"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12677556"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15770229"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21344540"}]}, "note": {"texts": [{"value": "The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry"}]}}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 715, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "BBSome complex member BBS7", "featureId": "PRO_0000064846"}, {"type": "Modified residue", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "N-acetylmethionine", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0007744", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22814378"}]}, {"type": "Alternative sequence", "location": {"start": {"value": 673, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 715, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "in isoform 2", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12567324"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "14702039"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15489334"}], "featureId": "VSP_008850", "alternativeSequence": {}}, {"type": "Natural variant", "location": {"start": {"value": 63, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 63, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "in BBS7; dbSNP:rs754579374", "featureCrossReferences": [{"database": "dbSNP", "id": "rs754579374"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21344540"}], "featureId": "VAR_066286", "alternativeSequence": {"originalSequence": "G", "alternativeSequences": ["